On 11 Oct 2005 12:37:04 -0700, W Marsh wrote:

> W Marsh wrote:
>> How do
>> I get rid of it? It's annoying  having to keep moving it into the
>> corner when my console window is in full screen mode.
> 
> The mouse cursor, that is. It seems erroneous that !mouse_support would
> be completely ignored.

tty interface by definition does not even know it is in a window - it could
be running out a serial port. The libraries don't have any knowledge of the
windows (or X) mouse pointer.

That said, you could almost certainly control the mouse pointer from a
commandline program for your system, and use a batch file to turn it off,
run Slashem, and turn it back on again when done.


